# Anaphora whose latest reading is contested (tasks.org,
# aida-referents-anaphora). "A queen walks. A knight walks silently. He
# whistles." The knight's argument presumes he does not whistle; the
# pronoun's reading for the knight presumes he does, so neither holds and
# the scaffold falls back to the queen.
lk.
pipeline unfolded.
declare iota : type.
declare knight,queen,whistles,walks : iota -> bool.
argument queen_walks : [!a:iota](exists x:iota, queen [x] - ~walks [x]).
elim [!a].
by default.
dixi.
argument knight_walks_silently : [!a:iota](exists x:iota, knight [x] - ~walks [x] - whistles [x]).
elim [!a].
elim.
by default.
next.
elim.
by default.
next.
by default.
dixi.
argument he_whistles : [?c:iota](exists x:iota, whistles [x]).
elim [?c].
by default.
dixi.
